WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.190
- And did you love, like,
playing your character?

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.810
You felt personally kinda connected

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:04.643
to being able to do this, right?

00:00:04.643 --> 00:00:06.000
- I felt hugely connected.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:07.260
I felt hugely connected

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.450
because the breakdown of the
character in the audition

00:00:09.450 --> 00:00:13.530
is, she's maternal,
and she brings some joy

00:00:13.530 --> 00:00:15.060
and, you know-

00:00:15.060 --> 00:00:15.900
- [Kelly] And you sing.

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:17.713
- And I sing.
- Yeah, you do.

00:00:20.490 --> 00:00:21.570
- Yeah, so for me

00:00:21.570 --> 00:00:23.760
it just felt like a really iconic moment.

00:00:23.760 --> 00:00:27.090
She is the first female dwarf
to have ever truly been seen

00:00:27.090 --> 00:00:29.520
within the world of
Tolkein or this franchise.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:31.080
She is the first dwarf of color

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:33.727
to have ever been seen
within this franchise.

00:00:33.727 --> 00:00:34.560
(audience applauding)

00:00:34.560 --> 00:00:36.472
- Yeah.
- Thank you.

00:00:36.472 --> 00:00:39.360
And so it felt like a moment to rise

00:00:39.360 --> 00:00:42.150
and I was very, very pregnant
at the time of auditioning,

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:44.610
and so, yeah, it's been a whole-

00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:46.910
- My God, I hated working
when I was pregnant.

00:00:48.870 --> 00:00:51.000
- Two days away from giving
birth before audition.

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:52.650
- What?
- Baby engaged,

00:00:52.650 --> 00:00:53.483
midwives on speed-dial.

00:00:53.483 --> 00:00:55.290
- The diaphragm has left.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:57.283
- I'm doing the camera test like this.

00:00:57.283 --> 00:00:58.543
(laughing)

00:00:58.543 --> 00:01:00.750
- I mean, what about
costumes, was that an issue?

00:01:00.750 --> 00:01:01.620
- Costumes?

00:01:01.620 --> 00:01:04.500
Can I just say the
first conversation I had

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:07.657
with the design team, she said,

00:01:07.657 --> 00:01:09.277
"You're breastfeeding, right?"

00:01:09.277 --> 00:01:10.410
"What do you need?"

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.187
- First of all, I love
that someone just said,

00:01:12.187 --> 00:01:14.153
"So you're breastfeeding"

00:01:14.153 --> 00:01:15.127
(audience clapping)
- Yeah

00:01:15.127 --> 00:01:16.320
- But that's so helpful

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:18.060
'cause people don't think about that.

00:01:18.060 --> 00:01:19.650
- So if there's pictures on my costume

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:22.290
but there's like these
stitching on, on the shoulders

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.981
and that was literally
in between takes me going

00:01:24.981 --> 00:01:27.330
so what is it, what are we saying?

00:01:27.330 --> 00:01:30.060
(all laughing)
(clapping)

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:31.890
- I love that that's
kind of your character

00:01:31.890 --> 00:01:32.760
in the film too, though.
- Yeah.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:34.800
- She's kinda like very
nurturing and funny

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.870
and it just, it's a
really great character.

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.520
- I appreciate it, thank you.
- I love y'all's relationship.

00:01:38.520 --> 00:01:39.353
It's so cool.

